Z||000003||Patrick||01-04-2000||02:34 AM||||<BR>454, you're talking about linking to an existing website. That doesn't help any of us who don't have a site of our own to post our wav files at. We used to have the same problem with images here until Cliff created <B>Pennock's Image Poster</B>. <P>I've suggested to Cliff in the past that it would be great to also be able to post wav files here. I believe Cliff's concern is the greater size of the files and the amount of storage space eventually required.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||01-04-2000||05:21 AM||||That's correct. WAV files are uncompressed and have a habit of being very large in size. But that doesn't mean I will never consider it. If enough people would find it an important addition to the forum, I will most certainly try to find a way to get it done.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||01-04-2000||10:32 AM||||Heres a tip.  If you dont have your own website space provided by your ISP, sign up for a free site on places like geocites, NetCenter, etc.  I use netcenter to store the pictures I post when I auction something.  Its easy and free and you could use it to store the wav files.  You'll have to manage your own space, but thats a small price to pay for adding waves to the forum. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Greg Piet||01-04-2000||12:31 PM||||What about using RealPlayer or mp3 format?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tom88gt||01-04-2000||02:04 PM||||Greg,<P>Buy a stethascope from and autoparts store. $10.  this will tell you more about your knock than anything else.||||reg||4
Z||000008||Scott2M4||01-12-2000||05:58 AM||||Greg's suggestion of using MP3 is a good idea.  A comparable MP3 file can be about 1/10th the size of a WAV file - and there's no noticeable degradation in sound quality after it's been compressed.<P>If Cliff considers this, he could allow MP3 only and leave the conversion of the WAV file to the end user.<P>Of course, that's where a recorder/converter like Audiograbber or MusicMatch and a player like Winamp would come in ...<p>[This message has been edited by Scott2M4 (edited 01-12-2000).]||||reg||1
